	dashiell@NADC.NADC.NAVY.MIL (A. Kaniss) writes:

 >How do you group multiple potions into one slot?

Just drop on the same spot.
Items won't group if they are different:
	in curse/bless status
	in identification status
	in enchantment status
	in naming status
	(... possibly more... I can't recall)

For example, you can have upto 6 groups for potions of water:
	2 potions of water		(unidentified, uncursed)
	2 potions of water		(unidentified, cursed)
	2 potions of water		(unidentified, blessed)
	2 uncursed potions of water	(identified, uncursed)
	2 potions of unholy water	(identified, cursed)
	2 potions of holy water		(identified, blessed)

Minor spoiler ahead:

If you drop all these potions of water on a Lawful alter,
you'll get
	12 potions of holy water
because they all get blessed and identified (unless you
are blind).
